// bisect: divergence — and here the INTERP is the wrong one.
// Found by soak aug14c (hz0 fuzz divergence_000000/000001, katana-class
// sibling), 2026-08-14, campaign binary 0b7fd7ef; survives the
// sleep-ride fix (0ba39657). Reduced by the fuzzer to 220 bytes, then
// by hand to the single ingredient below.
//
//   interp: Trace([0:i64:2 3:i64:2 4:i64:2])
//   jit:    Trace([0:i64:2 1:i64:7 2:i64:7 3:i64:2 4:i64:2])
//
// x iterates 1,2,3,4 so m = x/3 = 0,0,1,1, and the guard `m == i64:0`
// is true,true,false,false. The JIT's 2,7,7,2,2 is what the ruled
// semantics predict (init emits the `_` arm, then each m delivery fires
// the select and emits the taken arm's current value). The INTERP drops
// both guard-true productions entirely.
//
// The trigger is EXACTLY a `let` in the arm body, under recursion:
//   {let a = i64:3; a + i64:4}    DIVERGES
//   {let a = i64:3; let b = i64:4; a + b}  DIVERGES
//   (i64:3 + i64:4)              agrees
//   i64:3 + i64:4                agrees
//   i64:7                        agrees
// and the same program with `let f` instead of `let rec f` (no frame)
// agrees for every one of those bodies.
//
// ROOT CAUSE (confirmed 2026-08-14, GXDBG_REF=1 + shell bisect):
// two rules meet and drop the value channel on the floor.
//   1. `Constant::update` (node/mod.rs:644) checks FRAME DEPTH BEFORE
//      `event.init`, by design (gtailr epoch 2) — so inside a recursion
//      frame a constant delivers STALE even under the arm-wake's forced
//      init view (node/select.rs:388).
//   2. `Bind::update` (node/bind.rs:198) publishes only TRIGGERING
//      productions, on the premise that a stale RHS is "already served
//      by the bound names' store entries".
// That premise fails for an arm-local whose RHS is constant-only and
// whose arm was ASLEEP during the one genuine-init dispatch: it was
// never published, so there is no store entry to serve. The read then
// misses outright — `REF BindId(2790) MISS ride tag=Tag(96)` — rides a
// phantom bottom, the block bottoms, and the select has no arm value.
//
// Bisect receipts (recursive shell probe, interp vs jit):
//   {let a = X; a}       interp: 2 2        jit: X X 2 2   <-- read
//   {let a = X; i64:5}   interp: 5 5 2 2    jit: same      <-- unread
//   i64:7 / (3+4)        interp: 7 7 2 2    jit: same      <-- no bind
//   non-recursive        agree in every shape (genuine init reaches it)
//
// RECOMMENDED FIX: `Bind::update` materializes the value channel on its
// FIRST value-bearing production regardless of tag (publish with the
// honest tag, no notify) — dense R3's "producers write on genuine
// production, any tag". Publishing EVERY stale production would also
// work and is more uniform, but costs a store write per bind per cycle.
//
// Attribution: PRE-EXISTING, not today's work. On ac432b6a (this
// morning's tree, pre-organic-firing) the same program already
// diverges — interp [0:2 3:2] vs jit [0:2 1:7 3:7]. Organic firing
// changed the CADENCE on both sides (5 events now, 3 then) but not the
// class: the interp has never emitted the guard-true arm here.
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:3, i64:4]); let m = x / i64:3; let rec f = |n| select n {i64:0 => select i64:0 {i64:0 if m == i64:0 => {let a = i64:3; a + i64:4}, _ => i64:2}, _ => f(n - i64:1)}; f(i64:3)}
